A||||3||Tweek||turbo vs supercharger||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||06-10-2001||08:32 PM||||Would someone care to explain in laymans terms what the difference is between a turbo and a supercharger? I had always thought that it was 2 names for the same thing, but apparently not..  Thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fyerstarter||06-10-2001||08:52 PM||||A turbocharger is a little turbine that hooks up to your exhaust. It uses the pressure of your exhaust gases to compress the air coming in on the intake side. The more dense air the more fuel can be burned and the more power.<P>A supercharger works on the same principle of compressing air but it instead runs off of a belt and pulley system connected to your crank (just like AC, power steering, alternator, etc.) which runs a pump, which compresses the air.......<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tweek||06-10-2001||09:22 PM||||Ahh.... So a turbo would require less work to install...||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||06-10-2001||09:50 PM||||No not really. You need to plumb the exhaust and intake to get to the turbo.<P>With either system you need a different fuel managment system. A different MAP sensor and a way to retard the timing under boost conditions.||||reg||1
